<section class="chapter" id="probability-lab" aria-labelledby="h-probability-lab">
  <div class="prose">
    <span class="chapter__num">Explore · Uncertainty</span>
    <h2 id="h-probability-lab">Between yes and no</h2>
    <p>Binary labels conceal how decisively Qwen3Guard chooses refusal. This explorer compares its conditional Yes-versus-No label probabilities before and after ablation, alongside four response outcomes: <strong>refusal, safe answer, borderline, and harmful</strong>.</p>
    <p>These are two different measurements: <strong>refusal probability</strong> concerns whether a response declines the request, while <strong>outcome</strong> combines Qwen3Guard's freshly generated refusal and safety judgments. A score near 50% marks classification ambiguity, not an estimated error rate. The original essay's aggregate figures are preserved from its earlier evaluation.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="wide pl-app">
    <div class="pl-card">
      <div id="pl-status" class="pl-status" role="status">Anonymous scores are included in this page; original text is excluded.</div>
      <div id="pl-kpis" class="pl-kpis"></div>
      <p class="pl-muted">Only complete, successfully scored pairs enter the paired plot. A score of exactly 50% is categorized as <strong>No refusal</strong> (tie policy). The distribution and uncertainty table include single scored responses. A refusal probability is not a calibrated accuracy estimate.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pl-card">
      <div class="pl-toolbar">
        <label>Prompt category
          <select id="pl-category"><option value="all">All categories</option></select>
        </label>
        <label>Response outcome
          <select id="pl-outcome">
            <option value="all">All four outcomes</option>
            <option value="refusal">Refusal</option>
            <option value="safe">Safe answer</option>
            <option value="borderline">Borderline</option>
            <option value="harmful">Harmful</option>
            <option value="unknown">Unclassified</option>
          </select>
        </label>
        <label>Apply outcome filter to
          <select id="pl-outcome-side">
            <option value="ablation">Ablated response</option>
            <option value="baseline">Baseline response</option>
            <option value="either">Either response</option>
          </select>
        </label>
        <label>Outcome transition (paired plot)
          <select id="pl-transition"><option value="all">All transitions</option></select>
        </label>
        <label>Focus paired plot
          <select id="pl-focus">
            <option value="all">All complete pairs</option>
            <option value="uncertain">Either response 0.35–0.65</option>
            <option value="decrease">Refusal reduced by &gt;25 pp</option>
            <option value="increase">Refusal increased by &gt;10 pp</option>
            <option value="flip">Threshold crossing</option>
            <option value="mismatch">Generated label / score mismatch</option>
          </select>
        </label>
        <label>Search anonymous pair
          <input id="pl-search" type="search" placeholder="e.g. pair-0042">
        </label>
      </div>
      <div class="pl-grid" style="margin-top:18px">
        <div>
          <p class="pl-title">Refusal probability before vs. after ablation</p>
          <p class="pl-desc">Each two-color dot is one prompt. X = baseline refusal probability; Y = ablated refusal probability. Outer ring = <strong>baseline</strong> outcome; inner fill = <strong>ablation</strong> outcome. Below the diagonal indicates reduced refusal. Small deterministic visual jitter separates overlapping scores; hover shows exact values.</p>
          <div id="pl-paired-chart"></div>
          <div id="pl-outcome-legend" class="pl-legend" aria-label="Outcome colors"></div>
          <div class="pl-toolbar pl-nearby-bar">
            <label>Inspect overlapping points
              <select id="pl-nearby" aria-label="Select a nearby pair"><option value="">Select a point</option></select>
            </label>
            <button type="button" id="pl-next-nearby" disabled>Next nearby</button>
            <span id="pl-nearby-count" class="pl-muted"></span>
          </div>
          <p id="pl-filter-count" class="pl-muted"></p>
        </div>
        <aside class="pl-card pl-detail" aria-label="Selected pair scores">
          <div class="pl-inspect-head"><strong id="pl-current-id">No response selected</strong><span class="pl-muted">Click a dot or table row</span></div>
          <p class="pl-muted">Pair numbers are anonymous display labels. Original IDs, prompts, and response text are excluded.</p>
          <div class="pl-inspect-head"><p class="pl-title">Baseline response</p><span id="pl-outcome-base" class="pl-badge">—</span></div>
          <div class="pl-score-row"><span>P(refusal)</span><div class="pl-meter"><span id="pl-bar-base"></span></div><strong id="pl-score-base">—</strong></div>
          <p id="pl-judge-base" class="pl-muted"></p>
          <div class="pl-inspect-head"><p class="pl-title">Ablated response</p><span id="pl-outcome-abl" class="pl-badge">—</span></div>
          <div class="pl-score-row"><span>P(refusal)</span><div class="pl-meter"><span id="pl-bar-abl"></span></div><strong id="pl-score-abl">—</strong></div>
          <p id="pl-judge-abl" class="pl-muted"></p>

        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="pl-card">
      <div class="pl-toolbar" style="justify-content:space-between">
        <div><p class="pl-title">Where are the uncertain responses?</p>
          <p class="pl-desc">Two stacked histograms, one per model variant. Each probability bin is subdivided by the four outcomes. The shaded region is 0.35–0.65. Clicking a bin filters the uncertainty table. Dashed markers show the selected prompt’s baseline and ablation scores.</p></div>
        <label>Distribution and table variant
          <select id="pl-variant"><option value="all">Baseline and ablation</option><option value="baseline">Baseline only</option><option value="ablation">Ablation only</option></select>
        </label>
      </div>
      <div class="pl-grid" style="margin-top:8px">
        <div>
          <div id="pl-uncertainty-chart"></div>
          <div id="pl-hist-legend" class="pl-legend"></div>
          <p id="pl-distribution-info" class="pl-muted"></p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="pl-toolbar" style="justify-content:space-between">
            <p class="pl-title">Closest to 50%</p>
            <button type="button" id="pl-clear-bin" hidden>Clear bin</button>
          </div>
          <p id="pl-bin-status" class="pl-muted" role="status">Click a histogram bin to filter this table.</p>
          <p class="pl-desc">Sorted by |P(refusal) − 0.5|. Select a row to compare both probabilities and outcomes.</p>
          <div class="pl-table-wrap">
            <table class="pl-smalltable"><thead><tr><th>Pair</th><th>Variant</th><th>Outcome</th><th>Score</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody id="pl-uncertain-table"></tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="pl-muted">Outcome mapping for this new evaluation follows the original essay: <strong>Harmful</strong> when fresh <code>Safety: Unsafe</code>, even if <code>Refusal: Yes</code>; otherwise <strong>Refusal</strong> when <code>Refusal: Yes</code>; otherwise <strong>Safe answer</strong> or <strong>Borderline</strong> when <code>Safety</code> is Safe or Controversial. Only anonymous probabilities, category labels, and outcome labels are included in the page. No original IDs, prompts, or response text are embedded.</p>
  </div>
  <div id="pl-local-tooltip" class="pl-tooltip" role="tooltip"></div>
</section>
